# Claude factory: one line per repo the dispatcher picks cards for.
#   <repo folder> <Linear project>
# The folder is a git clone (~ is allowed). The project is the Linear project
# name whose Ready For Factory cards belong to that repo. Every line is
# commented out here on purpose: an uncommented line means this machine starts
# claiming that project's cards, so add only the repos you run.
#
# This machine's Linear label, added with `factory` to every card it picks up
# (kevin-omarchy or keith-omarchy):
# label kevin-omarchy
#
# Both machines can list the same projects. Each picks cards assigned to its
# owner or unassigned, and one machine waits before picking so they never
# claim at the same moment: Kevin 0, Keith 150 (seconds).
# offset 0
#
# Open PRs the factory didn't build are reviewed by the machine of whoever
# opened them: by default the GitHub login gh runs as here. List logins to
# replace that (never the same login on both machines). Add dependabot (on
# one machine only) to also check Dependabot's PRs for supply-chain signals;
# that reviewer comments and never pushes or merges:
# review-authors kkreative keithcatalyst dependabot
#
# The model each job runs on: "model <job> <model>", one line per job you
# change; a job with no line runs on its default (letters, digits, dots and
# dashes only). Builders follow the card's Risk section: build-low for Low,
# build-medium for Medium, build-high for High or a missing or unclear Risk.
# review is every PR reviewer except Dependabot's (dep-review); housekeeping is
# the Linear pick, settle and needs-merge calls. The defaults:
# model build-high claude-opus-5-5
# model build-medium claude-opus-5-5
# model build-low claude-sonnet-5-5
# model review claude-sonnet-5-5
# model dep-review claude-haiku-5-5
# model housekeeping haiku
# To put builders and reviewers back on Opus, uncomment and use these three:
# model build-low claude-opus-5-5
# model review claude-opus-5-5
# model dep-review claude-opus-5-5
#
# Where each repo's factory stage comes from (CAT-1486). board (the default)
# reads the stages the Factory Board computes each tick, keeps the last answer
# when the board can't be read, and falls back to the CLAUDE.md line
# 'Factory stage: 2' when it has no answer. claude-md ignores the board (the
# rollback): only that CLAUDE.md line counts, so at most Low PRs self-merge.
# stages claude-md
#
# ~/Projects/catalyst-shift catalyst-shift-site
# ~/Projects/lbl-nextjs lbl-nextjs
# ~/Projects/nourish-enablement nourish-rep-enablement
